NEARS-1109 AC3.6 FAIL — stale _loadMoreFailed seals pagination on a NEW query
Build: 2318a4d1 (fix-cycle 2).  Device emulator-5556.  Store 12 'Fresh local'.
Surface: StoreItemSearchScreen (/search-store-item), store app-bar Search icon.

REPRO (fault injection OFF for the decisive step — backend fully healthy):
 1. query 'a' (20 matches, limit=10 => 2 pages); proxy 500 iff offset=2.
 2. scroll -> page 2 500s -> inline row appears (correct, AC3.1 behaves).
 3. proxy rule OFF (backend healthy again).
 4. submit a NEW query in the same screen.

OBSERVED (healthy backend, nothing failing):
 09:37:53.783 PASS 200  GET /api/v1/items/search?store_id=12&name=a&offset=1&limit=10  [n=10 total=20]
 ... 18 scroll gestures to the bottom ...
 items/search requests total: 1        <-- offset=2 NEVER FETCHED
 offset=2 requests:           0
 "Couldn't load more" row:    PRESENT  <-- error row on a list where NOTHING failed
 [WARN] paginated list lines: only the 2 INJECTED failures (09:32:31, 09:36:19).
                              NO third [WARN] for this scroll => _paginate() never ran
                              => the scroll listener is SEALED, not throwing.

Page 2 of the new query is silently dropped for the rest of the session.

ROOT CAUSE  paginated_list_view.dart didUpdateWidget (~line 95):
  if (widget.offset != null && widget.offset != oldWidget.offset) {   // <-- 1 -> 1 is NOT a change
      if (modelOffset < (oldWidget.offset ?? _offset ?? 1)) {
        _loadMoreFailed = false;   // NEARS-1109: "a refresh/new-search resets the error row"
      }
  }
_loadMoreFailed is cleared ONLY when the MODEL offset moves BACKWARDS. But when page 2
FAILS the controller never advances past 1, so a new query resets 1 -> 1: no change, the
branch never runs, the flag stays true forever.  _scrollListener gates on !_loadMoreFailed,
so pagination is sealed for every subsequent query in the session.

Asymmetry that hides it: if the previous page SUCCEEDED (model offset=2), the new query
moves 2 -> 1 (backwards) and DOES reset correctly. It only bites after a FAILED page --
i.e. exactly the path this ticket added.

================================================================================
BLAST RADIUS — the SAME stale flag also seals the STORE GRID (AC1/AC2 surface,
which PASSED in cycle 1). paginated_list_view.dart is SHARED by every store branch.

CLEAN CONTROLLED RUN (fresh app restart, store 12, emulator-5556):
 A. control, fault OFF  -> grid paginates normally:
      09:48:09 PASS 200 items/latest offset=1 n=13 total=21
      09:48:31 PASS 200 items/latest offset=2 n=8          <- page 2 loads fine
 B. fresh store screen, fault ON (500 iff offset=2):
      09:54:46 KILL-500 items/latest offset=2
      [FAIL] endpoint=/api/v1/items/latest http_status=500 type=ApiFailure
      [WARN] paginated list: onPaginate(2) failed, retry re-allowed (ApiFailure)
      -> inline row shown, cursor rolled back.  CORRECT (smoke passes).
 C. fault OFF (backend fully healthy).  Tap category 'General Items' (resets page 1):
      09:55:18 PASS 200 items/latest category_id=1 offset=1 n=1 total=1
      "Couldn't load more" row STILL SHOWING on a healthy 1-item category.
 D. Tap category 'All' (21 items => page 2 exists), fault still OFF:
      09:55:37 PASS 200 items/latest category_id=0 offset=1 n=13 total=21
      ... 12 scroll gestures to the bottom ...
      offset=2 requests: 0        <- PAGE 2 NEVER FETCHED
      [WARN] paginated list lines: 0  <- _paginate() never ran => listener SEALED
      "Couldn't load more" row: PRESENT

RESULT: after ANY load-more failure, the store grid silently drops page 2 for the rest
of the session -- 8 of 21 items unreachable -- with a HEALTHY backend. This is the exact
bug class NEARS-1109 exists to fix, reintroduced by the NEARS-1109 fix itself, on the
same surface (AC1/AC2) that passed in cycle 1.

Unaffected: the 6 non-store PaginatedListView consumers (orders, home store list,
chat x2, conversations, flash-sale details). Their onPaginate never throws, so
_loadMoreFailed can never be raised -- byte-identical to pre-fix behaviour (verified).
